 34SI c  2003Iw02: a 38.4-MeV/nucleon, 2E10^4-pps, 99% pure {+34}Si secondary   
 34SI2c  beam was produced via the fragmentation of a 95-MeV/nucleon {+40}Ar    
 34SI3c  primary beam on a 2-mm-thick {+9}Be target separated by the RIKEN      
 34SI4c  projectile-fragment separator (RIPS). The secondary target was liquid  
 34SI5c  deuterium placed at the final achromatic focus F3 of RIPS. The reaction
 34SI6c  products were detected using four silicon counter telescopes each      
 34SI7c  consisting of four 500-|mm-thick ion-implanted silicon detectors.      
 34SI8c  Deexcitation |g rays were detected in coincidence with reaction        
 34SI9c  products by the DALI array of 68 NaI(Tl) scintillators. Measured E|g   
 34SIAc  with Doppler correction, I|g, |g|g-coin, and ({+34}Si)|g-coin.         
